# .gitignore-public — the internal/public boundary, in one place.
#
# Paths listed here are INTERNAL: they stay on a private remote and are
# STRIPPED from the scrubbed snapshot that `atlas publish` pushes to the
# public GitHub remote. Keep this in sync with the pre-push guard
# (.githooks/pre-push). This is NOT a normal .gitignore (git does not read
# it) — it is consumed by `core/brain/publish.py`.
#
# Raw brain captures — per-run candidates, run logs, full investigation reports.
brain/inbox/
brain/logs/runs/
brain/analytics/deliverables/
brain/analytics/reports/

# Internal-only durable brain:
#   wiki/cases        — case pages embed raw IOCs
#   wiki/environments — client-provided environment baselines
#   memory, issue     — name cases / carry live IOCs
brain/wiki/cases/
brain/wiki/environments/
brain/memory/
brain/issue/

# Contributor PII (personal + work e-mail + GitHub identity).
brain/CONTRIBUTORS

# Internal cases (NOT on the public cases allowlist).
#
# No internal case is committed at present, so no prefix is listed — a stale
# prefix that matches nothing is worse than no prefix, since it lets a test
# claim boundary coverage that isn't real. If a new internal case is added
# under demo-cases/ or cases/, list its prefix here in both forms (the
# committed location is demo-cases/, not cases/; a path that does not exist
# is skipped by the scrub in core/brain/publish.py, so listing both costs
# nothing and survives either layout).
#
# Identifier scanning is deliberately NOT the guard here — see the comment on
# _SCAN_TREES in publish.py. Public case evidence legitimately contains IOCs,
# so scanning demo-cases/ would fail on the public datasets, not on a real
# leak.
